{"actor":"cli","data":{"note":{"claims":["c1"],"id":"n1","kind":"limitation","text":"GaussianNB came out higher than the paper (0.586 vs 0.511). On pixel data it is dominated by near-zero-variance background pixels, so it is very sensitive to scikit-learn's var_smoothing and to pixel scaling, neither pinned down by the paper. The tree models, insensitive to both, reproduce (RandomForest) or come close (DecisionTree)."}},"hash":"sha256:cf8547aa4eca958e8e392d1a7876ef954eb85cd43133b6026e8d31dcd15a9a81","prev":"sha256:5e99665f6f68c09a5a1ce88406ce401532c0e21cdce0de80bbb576d5b8caf78b","schema":1,"seq":30,"tool_version":"0.5.0","ts":"2026-10-23T14:14:05.372Z","type":"note.added"}
